SteamARM: MetalFX's temporal scaler for an upscale the shim hands over

kk_steamarm_upscale_temporal(VkCommandBuffer, const struct sa_mfxt_cmd *)
is exported (C ABI, default visibility) for SteamARM's Vulkan shim. A
Windows FFX DLL of SteamARM's records a game's FSR 3.1 / DLSS style upscale
as an ordinary vkCmdUpdateBuffer whose 320 bytes are a struct sa_mfxt_cmd
(vulkan/kk_mfx_temporal.h: the text of SteamARM's shim/mfx_temporal.h, with
every offset asserted); the shim calls this instead of the update and gives
its status back to the DLL in the same call, which runs the game's own
upscaler on anything but OK.

PROBE answers OK and writes caps_out (temporal; motion vectors at the
output's size, jittered motion vectors and content offsets on macOS 27;
reactive mask; private copy), driver_out (28) and max_scale_out (3.0 on an
M4) into the command it is given, or answers UNSUPPORTED. DESTROY drops the
context's scalers. ENCODE takes each image's Metal texture (a view where a
mutable image is asked for in another format of the same size; depth always
in its own) and refuses with nothing encoded: BAD_ARGS inside a render
pass, for an image missing, not an image of the device, or smaller than the
sizes; UNSUPPORTED for a secondary command buffer, conditional rendering, a
scale outside 1x..3x, a format or texture usage MetalFX does not take (the
formats it took under Metal's debug layer, MEASURED), macOS 27 features on
an older system; NO_SCALER when MetalFX makes none, or for a ninth made
within 10 s. Otherwise patch 14's sequence: the encoders end,
MTL4FXTemporalScaler is encoded into the render passes' Metal command
buffer with the game's jitter, motion vector scale, pre-exposure, reset and
depth direction unchanged (depthReversed and the scale always set:
MetalFX's defaults are YES and minus the input size), auto exposure for
AUTO_EXP or for HDR without an exposure texture, and after_metalfx makes
the next encoder wait for it; a command buffer that ends right after
MetalFX gets a small encoder at its end that waits for it and that later
work waits for. One scaler per context, formats, sizes and flags (its
history), at most 8, one unused for 2 s dropped when another is asked for;
what an encode uses (the scaler, views, the private texture) is kept by its
Metal command buffer until KosmicKrisp releases that, when the GPU has
finished it. A command buffer that may be submitted again keeps the
command in its queue and encodes it again when it is recorded again.

KosmicKrisp's textures are shared, and MetalFX writes those correctly (the
same RMSE as private ones), but Metal's debug layer stops the process at
"outputTexture must have private storage mode". KK_MFXT_SCRATCH=1 (on by
itself with MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1) has MetalFX write a private texture of its
own, copied into the output, as an output without shader-write usage always
does: 1.04 ms per upscale written directly against 1.36 ms with the copy,
960x540 -> 1920x1080 RGBA16F, three frames in flight (MEASURED, M4,
2026-10-04). KK_MFXT=0: UNSUPPORTED always.

Tests (MEASURED 2026-10-04), SteamARM's tests/kk/run.sh: the bridge with
textures made as KosmicKrisp makes them, the game's jitter RMSE 0.0241
against 0.1378 for the opposite sign and 0.0904 for none, its motion
vectors 0.0753 against 0.1268 (+v) and 0.1340 (none), the same through the
private copy; the entry in the built driver called as the shim calls it,
15 checks (probe, encode, a read in the next command buffer, a command
buffer submitted twice, the refusals, destroy), also under Metal's debug
layer. Vulkan tests 40/40.

Not done: sharpening (MetalFX has none: SHARPEN and sharpness are
ignored), sa_mfxt_tex.flags and the reserved words are ignored, a
secondary command buffer is refused rather than replayed, and nothing
calls the entry until the shim and the DLL do.
diff -ruN a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.h b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.h
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.h	2026-10-04 21:13:34
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.h	2026-10-04 21:13:34
@@ -26,4 +26,75 @@
                                 mtl_command_buffer *cmd_buf, mtl_texture *in,
                                 mtl_texture *out, uint32_t in_w, uint32_t in_h);
 
+/* SteamARM: MetalFX's temporal scaler (MTL4FXTemporalScaler), for a game's
+ * FSR 3.1 / DLSS style upscale handed over by SteamARM's Vulkan shim
+ * (vulkan/kk_mfx_temporal.c). One scaler, with its history, per context
+ * the game made, kept while it is used. */
+struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_tex {
+   mtl_texture *texture; /* NULL: absent */
+   uint32_t format;      /* MTLPixelFormat to use it as (a view); 0: its own */
+   uint32_t x, y;        /* where its content starts (macOS 27) */
+};
+
+struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_args {
+   uint64_t context;
+   struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_tex color, depth, motion, exposure, reactive,
+      output;
+   /* The picture in color and depth (and in motion, unless mv_display: then
+    * motion is out_w x out_h), and what MetalFX writes into output. */
+   uint32_t render_w, render_h, out_w, out_h;
+   /* As the game gives them to FSR or DLSS: MetalFX takes the same signs and
+    * units (MEASURED, see kk_mfx_temporal.c). */
+   float jitter_x, jitter_y, mv_scale_x, mv_scale_y, pre_exposure;
+   bool reset, depth_reversed, auto_exposure, mv_display, mv_jittered;
+};
+
+enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status {
+   MTL_MFXT_OK = 0,
+   MTL_MFXT_BAD_ARGS,    /* textures missing, sizes outside the textures */
+   MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED, /* formats, usage, scale, macOS, no Metal 4 MetalFX */
+   MTL_MFXT_NO_SCALER,   /* MetalFX made no scaler for it, or too many made */
+};
+
+struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_caps {
+   bool supported, mv_display, mv_jittered, offsets, reactive;
+   float min_scale, max_scale;
+};
+
+void mtl_metalfx_temporal_get_caps(mtl_device *device,
+                                   struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_caps *caps);
+
+/* KK_MFXT_SCRATCH=1: MetalFX writes a private texture of its own, copied
+ * into the output (Metal's debug layer refuses an output that is not
+ * private; KosmicKrisp's are shared, which MetalFX writes correctly). On by
+ * itself with MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 unless KK_MFXT_SCRATCH=0; an output without
+ * shader-write usage always goes this way. */
+bool mtl_metalfx_temporal_scratch(void);
+
+/* Whether mtl_metalfx_temporal_encode would take this (it makes and keeps
+ * the scaler): asked before the caller ends its encoders. *why: the reason
+ * of a refusal, for the log. */
+enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status
+mtl_metalfx_temporal_prepare(mtl_device *device, mtl_compiler *compiler,
+                             const struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_args *args,
+                             const char **why);
+
+/* Encodes the upscale into `cmd_buf` (a Metal 4 command buffer with no
+ * encoder open). What the GPU uses (the scaler, views, the private texture)
+ * is kept alive by the command buffer until Metal lets it go. */
+enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status
+mtl_metalfx_temporal_encode(mtl_device *device, mtl_compiler *compiler,
+                            mtl_command_buffer *cmd_buf,
+                            const struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_args *args,
+                            const char **why);
+
+/* The context is gone: its scalers are dropped (work already encoded keeps
+ * them until it has run). */
+void mtl_metalfx_temporal_destroy(uint64_t context);
+
+/* A small encoder that waits for all work before it and that later work
+ * waits for: put after MetalFX when nothing of the driver follows it in its
+ * command buffer, so later command buffers see MetalFX's writes. */
+void mtl_metalfx_temporal_tail(mtl_device *device, mtl_command_buffer *cmd_buf);
+
 #endif /* MTL_METALFX_H */
diff -ruN a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.m b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.m
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.m	2026-10-04 21:13:34
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.m	2026-10-04 21:13:34
@@ -166,3 +166,744 @@
    }
    return ok;
 }
+
+/* SteamARM: MetalFX's temporal scaler, for a game's FSR 3.1 / DLSS style
+ * upscale (vulkan/kk_mfx_temporal.c). What follows was measured on an M4
+ * with macOS 27 (MetalFX's own temporal scaler, Metal 4):
+ *  - scale 1x to exactly 3x a side; more, or a downscale, gets no scaler;
+ *  - inputs need only shader-read usage, the output shader-write (its
+ *    reported usage, 0x7, is more than it needs);
+ *  - outputs of shared storage, KosmicKrisp's, are written correctly (the
+ *    same picture as private ones), though Metal's debug layer refuses them
+ *    ("outputTexture must have private storage mode"): KK_MFXT_SCRATCH=1
+ *    gives MetalFX a private texture of its own and copies it;
+ *  - depthReversed defaults to YES and the motion vector scale to
+ *    (-inputWidth, -inputHeight): both always set here;
+ *  - making a scaler takes 60-490 ms (a new size or format the longest). */
+
+#include <objc/runtime.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <time.h>
+
+/* A context keeps its history in its scaler; a game has one or two (one
+ * per view, made again when the resolution changes). A few kept: the least
+ * recently used goes, and one unused for 2 s goes when another is asked
+ * for (a game that stops upscaling for a while finds its own again). */
+#define MFXT_ENTRIES 8
+#define MFXT_IDLE_S 2.0
+/* Past 8 made in 10 s a new one is refused: the game's own upscaler until
+ * then (patch 17: scalers made again and again stalled the game and took
+ * 7 GB). */
+#define MFXT_MAKE_BURST 8
+#define MFXT_MAKE_WINDOW_S 10.0
+
+struct mfxt_entry {
+   bool used;
+   id<MTLDevice> dev;
+   uint64_t context;
+   MTLPixelFormat cf, df, mf, of, rf; /* rf 0: no reactive mask */
+   NSUInteger in_w, in_h, out_w, out_h;
+   bool auto_exposure, mv_display, mv_jittered, scratch;
+   id<MTL4FXTemporalScaler> scaler; /* nil: refused, for `why` */
+   enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status status;
+   const char *why;
+   id<MTLTexture> scratch_tex;
+   id<MTLResidencySet> scratch_set;
+   double last_used;
+   bool fresh; /* nothing encoded yet: no history */
+};
+
+static struct mfxt_entry mfxt_entries[MFXT_ENTRIES];
+static double mfxt_made_at[MFXT_MAKE_BURST];
+static unsigned mfxt_made;
+static pthread_mutex_t mfxt_lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
+
+static double
+mfxt_now(void)
+{
+   struct timespec ts;
+   clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);
+   return ts.tv_sec + ts.tv_nsec * 1e-9;
+}
+
+static void
+mfxt_drop(struct mfxt_entry *e)
+{
+   [e->scaler release];
+   [e->scratch_tex release];
+   [e->scratch_set release];
+   memset(e, 0, sizeof(*e));
+}
+
+/* The formats MetalFX took, with correct values read back, under Metal's
+ * debug layer (MEASURED, M4, macOS 27). Others are not offered to it. */
+static const MTLPixelFormat mfxt_color_formats[] = {
+   MTLPixelFormatRGBA16Float, MTLPixelFormatRGBA8Unorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatRGBA8Unorm_sRGB, MTLPixelFormatRGBA8Snorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatBGRA8Unorm, MTLPixelFormatBGRA8Unorm_sRGB,
+   MTLPixelFormatRGB10A2Unorm, MTLPixelFormatBGR10A2Unorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatRG11B10Float, MTLPixelFormatRGB9E5Float,
+   MTLPixelFormatRGBA32Float, MTLPixelFormatRGBA16Unorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatRGBA16Snorm, MTLPixelFormatR16Unorm, MTLPixelFormatR32Float,
+};
+static const MTLPixelFormat mfxt_depth_formats[] = {
+   MTLPixelFormatDepth32Float, MTLPixelFormatDepth16Unorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatDepth32Float_Stencil8, MTLPixelFormatR32Float,
+   MTLPixelFormatR16Float,
+};
+static const MTLPixelFormat mfxt_motion_formats[] = {
+   MTLPixelFormatRG16Float, MTLPixelFormatRG32Float, MTLPixelFormatRG16Snorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatRG16Unorm, MTLPixelFormatRGBA16Float, MTLPixelFormatRG8Unorm,
+};
+static const MTLPixelFormat mfxt_output_formats[] = {
+   MTLPixelFormatRGBA16Float, MTLPixelFormatBGRA8Unorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatBGRA8Unorm_sRGB, MTLPixelFormatRGBA8Unorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatRGBA8Unorm_sRGB, MTLPixelFormatRGB10A2Unorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatBGR10A2Unorm, MTLPixelFormatRG11B10Float,
+   MTLPixelFormatRGBA32Float, MTLPixelFormatRGBA16Unorm,
+};
+static const MTLPixelFormat mfxt_reactive_formats[] = {
+   MTLPixelFormatR8Unorm, MTLPixelFormatR16Float, MTLPixelFormatR16Unorm,
+   MTLPixelFormatR32Float, MTLPixelFormatRG8Unorm, MTLPixelFormatRGBA8Unorm,
+};
+static const MTLPixelFormat mfxt_exposure_formats[] = {
+   MTLPixelFormatR16Float, MTLPixelFormatR32Float, MTLPixelFormatRG32Float,
+   MTLPixelFormatRGBA16Float, MTLPixelFormatRGBA32Float,
+};
+
+static bool
+mfxt_format_in(MTLPixelFormat f, const MTLPixelFormat *list, unsigned n)
+{
+   for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++)
+      if (list[i] == f)
+         return true;
+   return false;
+}
+
+static void
+mfxt_caps_locked(id<MTLDevice> dev, struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_caps *caps)
+{
+   static id<MTLDevice> cached_dev;
+   static struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_caps cached;
+   if (cached_dev != dev) {
+      memset(&cached, 0, sizeof(cached));
+      cached.supported = [MTLFXTemporalScalerDescriptor supportsDevice:dev] &&
+                         [MTLFXTemporalScalerDescriptor supportsMetal4FX:dev];
+      if (cached.supported) {
+         cached.min_scale =
+            [MTLFXTemporalScalerDescriptor supportedInputContentMinScaleForDevice:dev];
+         cached.max_scale =
+            [MTLFXTemporalScalerDescriptor supportedInputContentMaxScaleForDevice:dev];
+         if (cached.min_scale < 1.0f)
+            cached.min_scale = 1.0f;
+         cached.reactive = true;
+         if (@available(macOS 27.0, *))
+            cached.mv_display = cached.mv_jittered = cached.offsets = true;
+      }
+      cached_dev = dev;
+   }
+   *caps = cached;
+}
+
+void
+mtl_metalfx_temporal_get_caps(mtl_device *device,
+                              struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_caps *caps)
+{
+   @autoreleasepool {
+      pthread_mutex_lock(&mfxt_lock);
+      mfxt_caps_locked((id<MTLDevice>)device, caps);
+      pthread_mutex_unlock(&mfxt_lock);
+   }
+}
+
+bool
+mtl_metalfx_temporal_scratch(void)
+{
+   /* On by itself under Metal's debug layer (MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1), which
+    * otherwise stops the process at the first encode; KK_MFXT_SCRATCH=0
+    * turns it off even then. */
+   static int on = -1;
+   if (on < 0) {
+      const char *e = getenv("KK_MFXT_SCRATCH");
+      const char *d = getenv("MTL_DEBUG_LAYER");
+      on = e ? e[0] == '1' : (d && d[0] == '1');
+   }
+   return on;
+}
+
+struct mfxt_tex {
+   id<MTLTexture> t; /* nil: absent */
+   MTLPixelFormat f; /* what MetalFX is told */
+   NSUInteger x, y;
+};
+
+/* One texture: a plain 2D one (or the first layer of a 2D array), a format
+ * MetalFX takes (a view in another format only where the texture allows
+ * one), its content within it, readable by shaders unless it is the
+ * output. */
+static enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status
+mfxt_tex_check(const struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_tex *in,
+               const MTLPixelFormat *list, unsigned n, NSUInteger need_w,
+               NSUInteger need_h, bool output, struct mfxt_tex *out,
+               const char **why)
+{
+   id<MTLTexture> t = (id<MTLTexture>)in->texture;
+   out->t = t;
+   out->f = in->format ? (MTLPixelFormat)in->format : t.pixelFormat;
+   out->x = in->x;
+   out->y = in->y;
+   if (t.textureType != MTLTextureType2D &&
+       t.textureType != MTLTextureType2DArray) {
+      *why = "a texture that is not plain 2D";
+      return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+   }
+   if (out->f != t.pixelFormat && !(t.usage & MTLTextureUsagePixelFormatView)) {
+      *why = "a view in another format of a texture that allows none";
+      return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+   }
+   if (!mfxt_format_in(out->f, list, n)) {
+      *why = "a format MetalFX does not take";
+      return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+   }
+   if (out->x + need_w > t.width || out->y + need_h > t.height) {
+      *why = "sizes outside the textures";
+      return MTL_MFXT_BAD_ARGS;
+   }
+   if (!output && !(t.usage & MTLTextureUsageShaderRead)) {
+      *why = "an input shaders cannot read";
+      return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+   }
+   return MTL_MFXT_OK;
+}
+
+#define MFXT_N(list) (unsigned)(sizeof(list) / sizeof(list[0]))
+
+/* Checks everything and finds (or makes) the scaler. Caller holds the
+ * lock. tx: color, depth, motion, exposure, reactive, output. */
+static enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status
+mfxt_prepare_locked(id<MTLDevice> dev, id<MTL4Compiler> compiler,
+                    const struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_args *a,
+                    struct mfxt_tex tx[6], struct mfxt_entry **entry,
+                    const char **why)
+{
+   enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status st;
+   struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_caps caps;
+   mfxt_caps_locked(dev, &caps);
+   memset(tx, 0, 6 * sizeof(tx[0]));
+   *entry = NULL;
+
+   if (!caps.supported) {
+      *why = "no Metal 4 MetalFX temporal scaler on this GPU";
+      return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+   }
+   if (!a->color.texture || !a->depth.texture || !a->motion.texture ||
+       !a->output.texture) {
+      *why = "colour, depth, motion vectors or output missing";
+      return MTL_MFXT_BAD_ARGS;
+   }
+   if (!a->render_w || !a->render_h || !a->out_w || !a->out_h) {
+      *why = "a size of 0";
+      return MTL_MFXT_BAD_ARGS;
+   }
+   if (a->out_w < a->render_w || a->out_h < a->render_h) {
+      *why = "a downscale";
+      return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+   }
+   /* A near-native request (FSR Native AA) on a GPU whose smallest scale is
+    * above 1: MetalFX would reject the content scale at encode. */
+   if ((double)a->out_w < (double)a->render_w * caps.min_scale - 1e-3 ||
+       (double)a->out_h < (double)a->render_h * caps.min_scale - 1e-3) {
+      *why = "less than MetalFX's smallest scale";
+      return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+   }
+   if ((double)a->out_w > (double)a->render_w * caps.max_scale + 1e-3 ||
+       (double)a->out_h > (double)a->render_h * caps.max_scale + 1e-3) {
+      *why = "more than MetalFX's largest scale";
+      return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+   }
+   if ((a->mv_display && !caps.mv_display) ||
+       (a->mv_jittered && !caps.mv_jittered)) {
+      *why = "motion vectors at the output's size or jittered (macOS 27)";
+      return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+   }
+   const struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_tex *in[6] = {
+      &a->color, &a->depth, &a->motion, &a->exposure, &a->reactive, &a->output,
+   };
+   for (unsigned i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
+      /* MetalFX reads the exposure from its texture's first texel. */
+      if (in[i]->texture && (in[i]->x || in[i]->y) &&
+          (!caps.offsets || i == 3)) {
+         *why = "content away from the textures' origin (macOS 27)";
+         return MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+      }
+   }
+   NSUInteger mv_w = a->mv_display ? a->out_w : a->render_w;
+   NSUInteger mv_h = a->mv_display ? a->out_h : a->render_h;
+   if ((st = mfxt_tex_check(&a->color, mfxt_color_formats,
+                            MFXT_N(mfxt_color_formats), a->render_w,
+                            a->render_h, false, &tx[0], why)) ||
+       (st = mfxt_tex_check(&a->depth, mfxt_depth_formats,
+                            MFXT_N(mfxt_depth_formats), a->render_w,
+                            a->render_h, false, &tx[1], why)) ||
+       (st = mfxt_tex_check(&a->motion, mfxt_motion_formats,
+                            MFXT_N(mfxt_motion_formats), mv_w, mv_h, false,
+                            &tx[2], why)) ||
+       (a->exposure.texture &&
+        (st = mfxt_tex_check(&a->exposure, mfxt_exposure_formats,
+                             MFXT_N(mfxt_exposure_formats), 1, 1, false,
+                             &tx[3], why))) ||
+       (a->reactive.texture &&
+        (st = mfxt_tex_check(&a->reactive, mfxt_reactive_formats,
+                             MFXT_N(mfxt_reactive_formats), a->render_w,
+                             a->render_h, false, &tx[4], why))) ||
+       (st = mfxt_tex_check(&a->output, mfxt_output_formats,
+                            MFXT_N(mfxt_output_formats), a->out_w, a->out_h,
+                            true, &tx[5], why)))
+      return st;
+   if (tx[1].f != tx[1].t.pixelFormat) {
+      *why = "depth in a format of its own";
+      return MTL_MFXT_BAD_ARGS;
+   }
+
+   /* The input size: the colour texture's (its content may be smaller,
+    * inputContentWidth/Height each frame: a dynamic resolution keeps the
+    * scaler), no larger than the output. */
+   NSUInteger in_w = MIN(tx[0].t.width - tx[0].x, (NSUInteger)a->out_w);
+   NSUInteger in_h = MIN(tx[0].t.height - tx[0].y, (NSUInteger)a->out_h);
+   bool scratch = mtl_metalfx_temporal_scratch() ||
+                  !(tx[5].t.usage & MTLTextureUsageShaderWrite);
+   MTLPixelFormat rf = tx[4].t ? tx[4].f : MTLPixelFormatInvalid;
+   double now = mfxt_now();
+
+   struct mfxt_entry *e = NULL, *free_e = NULL, *lru = NULL;
+   for (unsigned i = 0; i < MFXT_ENTRIES; i++) {
+      struct mfxt_entry *c = &mfxt_entries[i];
+      if (c->used && c->dev == dev && c->context == a->context &&
+          c->cf == tx[0].f && c->df == tx[1].f && c->mf == tx[2].f &&
+          c->of == tx[5].f && c->rf == rf && c->in_w == in_w &&
+          c->in_h == in_h && c->out_w == a->out_w && c->out_h == a->out_h &&
+          c->auto_exposure == a->auto_exposure &&
+          c->mv_display == a->mv_display && c->mv_jittered == a->mv_jittered &&
+          c->scratch == scratch) {
+         e = c;
+         break;
+      }
+   }
+   if (!e) {
+      for (unsigned i = 0; i < MFXT_ENTRIES; i++) {
+         struct mfxt_entry *c = &mfxt_entries[i];
+         if (c->used && now - c->last_used > MFXT_IDLE_S)
+            mfxt_drop(c);
+         if (!c->used) {
+            if (!free_e)
+               free_e = c;
+         } else if (!lru || c->last_used < lru->last_used) {
+            lru = c;
+         }
+      }
+
+      unsigned oldest = mfxt_made % MFXT_MAKE_BURST;
+      if (mfxt_made >= MFXT_MAKE_BURST &&
+          now - mfxt_made_at[oldest] < MFXT_MAKE_WINDOW_S) {
+         static double told;
+         if (now - told > MFXT_MAKE_WINDOW_S) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "kk: MetalFX temporal: %u scalers made in %.0f s, "
+                            "no more for now: the game's own upscaler\n",
+                    MFXT_MAKE_BURST, MFXT_MAKE_WINDOW_S);
+            told = now;
+         }
+         *why = "too many scalers made";
+         return MTL_MFXT_NO_SCALER;
+      }
+      mfxt_made_at[oldest] = now;
+      mfxt_made++;
+
+      e = free_e ? free_e : lru;
+      if (e->used)
+         mfxt_drop(e);
+
+      MTLFXTemporalScalerDescriptor *desc = [MTLFXTemporalScalerDescriptor new];
+      desc.colorTextureFormat = tx[0].f;
+      desc.depthTextureFormat = tx[1].f;
+      desc.motionTextureFormat = tx[2].f;
+      desc.outputTextureFormat = tx[5].f;
+      desc.inputWidth = in_w;
+      desc.inputHeight = in_h;
+      desc.outputWidth = a->out_w;
+      desc.outputHeight = a->out_h;
+      /* The picture smaller than the input textures each frame; also 12-15 %
+       * faster (MEASURED). */
+      desc.inputContentPropertiesEnabled = YES;
+      desc.inputContentMinScale = caps.min_scale;
+      desc.inputContentMaxScale = caps.max_scale;
+      desc.autoExposureEnabled = a->auto_exposure;
+      desc.requiresSynchronousInitialization = YES;
+      if (rf != MTLPixelFormatInvalid) {
+         desc.reactiveMaskTextureEnabled = YES;
+         desc.reactiveMaskTextureFormat = rf;
+      }
+      if (@available(macOS 27.0, *)) {
+         desc.outputResolutionMotionVectorsEnabled = a->mv_display;
+         desc.jitteredMotionVectorsEnabled = a->mv_jittered;
+      }
+      id<MTL4FXTemporalScaler> s =
+         [desc newTemporalScalerWithDevice:dev compiler:compiler];
+      [desc release];
+      double ms = (mfxt_now() - now) * 1000.0;
+
+      const char *refused = NULL;
+      enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status rst = MTL_MFXT_OK;
+      if (!s) {
+         refused = "MetalFX has no scaler for it";
+         rst = MTL_MFXT_NO_SCALER;
+      } else {
+         MTLTextureUsage ru = 0;
+         if (tx[4].t) {
+            if (@available(macOS 27.0, *)) {
+               ru = s.reactiveMaskTextureUsage;
+            } else {
+#pragma clang diagnostic push
+#pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Wdeprecated-declarations"
+               ru = s.reactiveTextureUsage; /* its name before macOS 27 */
+#pragma clang diagnostic pop
+            }
+         }
+         if ((tx[0].t.usage & s.colorTextureUsage) != s.colorTextureUsage ||
+             (tx[1].t.usage & s.depthTextureUsage) != s.depthTextureUsage ||
+             (tx[2].t.usage & s.motionTextureUsage) != s.motionTextureUsage ||
+             (tx[4].t && (tx[4].t.usage & ru) != ru)) {
+            refused = "texture usage MetalFX needs missing";
+            rst = MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+            [s release];
+            s = nil;
+         }
+      }
+
+      id<MTLTexture> stex = nil;
+      id<MTLResidencySet> sset = nil;
+      if (s && scratch) {
+         /* Its own residency set, never changed: one the queue's work still
+          * uses is never made non-resident under it. */
+         MTLTextureDescriptor *td = [MTLTextureDescriptor
+            texture2DDescriptorWithPixelFormat:tx[5].f
+                                         width:a->out_w
+                                        height:a->out_h
+                                     mipmapped:NO];
+         td.usage = s.outputTextureUsage | MTLTextureUsageShaderRead |
+                    MTLTextureUsageShaderWrite;
+         td.storageMode = MTLStorageModePrivate;
+         stex = [dev newTextureWithDescriptor:td];
+         MTLResidencySetDescriptor *rd = [MTLResidencySetDescriptor new];
+         rd.initialCapacity = 1;
+         NSError *err = nil;
+         sset = stex ? [dev newResidencySetWithDescriptor:rd error:&err] : nil;
+         [rd release];
+         if (sset) {
+            [sset addAllocation:stex];
+            [sset commit];
+            [sset requestResidency];
+         } else {
+            [stex release];
+            stex = nil;
+            [s release];
+            s = nil;
+            refused = "no private texture for the output";
+            rst = MTL_MFXT_NO_SCALER;
+         }
+      }
+
+      fprintf(stderr,
+              "kk: MetalFX temporal: context %llu: %lux%lu -> %lux%lu (colour "
+              "%lu, depth %lu, motion %lu%s, output %lu%s%s%s%s) in %.0f ms%s%s\n",
+              (unsigned long long)a->context, (unsigned long)in_w,
+              (unsigned long)in_h, (unsigned long)a->out_w,
+              (unsigned long)a->out_h, (unsigned long)tx[0].f,
+              (unsigned long)tx[1].f, (unsigned long)tx[2].f,
+              a->mv_display ? " at the output's size" : "",
+              (unsigned long)tx[5].f, scratch ? " through a private copy" : "",
+              rf != MTLPixelFormatInvalid ? ", reactive mask" : "",
+              a->auto_exposure ? ", auto exposure" : "",
+              a->mv_jittered ? ", jittered motion" : "", ms,
+              refused ? ": " : "", refused ? refused : "");
+
+      *e = (struct mfxt_entry){
+         .used = true,
+         .dev = dev,
+         .context = a->context,
+         .cf = tx[0].f,
+         .df = tx[1].f,
+         .mf = tx[2].f,
+         .of = tx[5].f,
+         .rf = rf,
+         .in_w = in_w,
+         .in_h = in_h,
+         .out_w = a->out_w,
+         .out_h = a->out_h,
+         .auto_exposure = a->auto_exposure,
+         .mv_display = a->mv_display,
+         .mv_jittered = a->mv_jittered,
+         .scratch = scratch,
+         .scaler = s,
+         .status = rst,
+         .why = refused,
+         .scratch_tex = stex,
+         .scratch_set = sset,
+         .fresh = true,
+      };
+   }
+   e->last_used = now;
+   if (!e->scaler) {
+      *why = e->why;
+      return e->status;
+   }
+   *entry = e;
+   return MTL_MFXT_OK;
+}
+
+enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status
+mtl_metalfx_temporal_prepare(mtl_device *device, mtl_compiler *compiler,
+                             const struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_args *args,
+                             const char **why)
+{
+   enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status st;
+   const char *dummy;
+   if (!why)
+      why = &dummy;
+   *why = NULL;
+   @autoreleasepool {
+      struct mfxt_tex tx[6];
+      struct mfxt_entry *e;
+      pthread_mutex_lock(&mfxt_lock);
+      st = mfxt_prepare_locked((id<MTLDevice>)device,
+                               (id<MTL4Compiler>)compiler, args, tx, &e, why);
+      pthread_mutex_unlock(&mfxt_lock);
+   }
+   return st;
+}
+
+/* Kept by the command buffer, released with it (KosmicKrisp releases its
+ * Metal command buffers when the GPU has finished them, or unsubmitted at a
+ * reset): Metal 4 command buffers do not retain what they use. */
+static char mfxt_keep_key;
+
+static void
+mfxt_keep(id<MTL4CommandBuffer> cb, id obj)
+{
+   if (!obj)
+      return;
+   NSMutableArray *keep = objc_getAssociatedObject(cb, &mfxt_keep_key);
+   if (!keep) {
+      keep = [NSMutableArray new];
+      objc_setAssociatedObject(cb, &mfxt_keep_key, keep,
+                               OBJC_ASSOCIATION_RETAIN_NONATOMIC);
+      [keep release];
+   }
+   [keep addObject:obj];
+}
+
+static bool
+mfxt_kept(id<MTL4CommandBuffer> cb, id obj)
+{
+   NSMutableArray *keep = objc_getAssociatedObject(cb, &mfxt_keep_key);
+   return keep && [keep indexOfObjectIdenticalTo:obj] != NSNotFound;
+}
+
+/* The texture as MetalFX is to see it: itself, or (another format, a layer
+ * of an array, mipmaps) a 2D view of its first level and layer. +1. */
+static id<MTLTexture>
+mfxt_view(const struct mfxt_tex *t)
+{
+   if (!t->t)
+      return nil;
+   if (t->f == t->t.pixelFormat && t->t.textureType == MTLTextureType2D &&
+       t->t.mipmapLevelCount == 1)
+      return [t->t retain];
+   return [t->t newTextureViewWithPixelFormat:t->f
+                                  textureType:MTLTextureType2D
+                                       levels:NSMakeRange(0, 1)
+                                       slices:NSMakeRange(0, 1)];
+}
+
+enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status
+mtl_metalfx_temporal_encode(mtl_device *device, mtl_compiler *compiler,
+                            mtl_command_buffer *cmd_buf,
+                            const struct mtl_metalfx_temporal_args *a,
+                            const char **why)
+{
+   enum mtl_metalfx_temporal_status st;
+   const char *dummy;
+   if (!why)
+      why = &dummy;
+   *why = NULL;
+
+   @autoreleasepool {
+      id<MTL4CommandBuffer> cb = (id<MTL4CommandBuffer>)cmd_buf;
+      struct mfxt_tex tx[6];
+      struct mfxt_entry *e;
+      id<MTLTexture> v[6] = {nil};
+
+      pthread_mutex_lock(&mfxt_lock);
+      st = mfxt_prepare_locked((id<MTLDevice>)device,
+                               (id<MTL4Compiler>)compiler, a, tx, &e, why);
+      if (st == MTL_MFXT_OK) {
+         for (unsigned i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
+            v[i] = mfxt_view(&tx[i]);
+            if (tx[i].t && !v[i]) {
+               *why = "no view of a texture in the format asked";
+               st = MTL_MFXT_UNSUPPORTED;
+            }
+         }
+      }
+      if (st == MTL_MFXT_OK) {
+         id<MTL4FXTemporalScaler> s = e->scaler;
+         s.colorTexture = v[0];
+         s.depthTexture = v[1];
+         s.motionTexture = v[2];
+         s.outputTexture = e->scratch ? e->scratch_tex : v[5];
+         /* Auto exposure ignores the texture; none means 1. */
+         s.exposureTexture = a->auto_exposure ? nil : v[3];
+         s.reactiveMaskTexture = e->rf != MTLPixelFormatInvalid ? v[4] : nil;
+         s.inputContentWidth = a->render_w;
+         s.inputContentHeight = a->render_h;
+         if (@available(macOS 27.0, *)) {
+            s.colorContentOffsetX = tx[0].x;
+            s.colorContentOffsetY = tx[0].y;
+            s.depthContentOffsetX = tx[1].x;
+            s.depthContentOffsetY = tx[1].y;
+            s.motionContentOffsetX = tx[2].x;
+            s.motionContentOffsetY = tx[2].y;
+            s.reactiveMaskContentOffsetX = tx[4].x;
+            s.reactiveMaskContentOffsetY = tx[4].y;
+            s.outputOffsetX = e->scratch ? 0 : tx[5].x;
+            s.outputOffsetY = e->scratch ? 0 : tx[5].y;
+         }
+         /* The game's values unchanged: MetalFX's jitter is the negated
+          * sample offset and its motion vectors point from the current
+          * position to the previous one, as FSR's and DLSS's (MEASURED with
+          * a supersampled reference: the other signs were worse than no
+          * jitter or no motion vectors at all). */
+         s.jitterOffsetX = a->jitter_x;
+         s.jitterOffsetY = a->jitter_y;
+         s.motionVectorScaleX = a->mv_scale_x;
+         s.motionVectorScaleY = a->mv_scale_y;
+         s.preExposure = a->pre_exposure > 0.0f ? a->pre_exposure : 1.0f;
+         s.depthReversed = a->depth_reversed;
+         s.reset = a->reset || e->fresh;
+         [s encodeToCommandBuffer:cb];
+         /* Encoded: the scaler need not keep the game's textures alive. */
+         s.colorTexture = nil;
+         s.depthTexture = nil;
+         s.motionTexture = nil;
+         s.outputTexture = nil;
+         s.exposureTexture = nil;
+         s.reactiveMaskTexture = nil;
+         e->fresh = false;
+
+         mfxt_keep(cb, s);
+         for (unsigned i = 0; i < 6; i++)
+            if (v[i] && v[i] != tx[i].t)
+               mfxt_keep(cb, v[i]);
+
+         if (e->scratch) {
+            if (!mfxt_kept(cb, e->scratch_set)) {
+               [cb useResidencySet:e->scratch_set];
+               mfxt_keep(cb, e->scratch_set);
+               mfxt_keep(cb, e->scratch_tex);
+            }
+            /* MetalFX's writes, then the copy into the game's output; what
+             * comes after waits for the copy. */
+            id<MTL4ComputeCommandEncoder> ce = [cb computeCommandEncoder];
+            [ce barrierAfterQueueStages:MTLStageAll
+                           beforeStages:MTLStageBlit
+                      visibilityOptions:MTL4VisibilityOptionDevice];
+            [ce copyFromTexture:e->scratch_tex
+                     sourceSlice:0
+                     sourceLevel:0
+                    sourceOrigin:MTLOriginMake(0, 0, 0)
+                      sourceSize:MTLSizeMake(a->out_w, a->out_h, 1)
+                       toTexture:v[5]
+                destinationSlice:0
+                destinationLevel:0
+               destinationOrigin:MTLOriginMake(tx[5].x, tx[5].y, 0)];
+            [ce barrierAfterStages:MTLStageBlit
+                 beforeQueueStages:MTLStageAll
+                 visibilityOptions:MTL4VisibilityOptionDevice];
+            [ce endEncoding];
+         }
+      }
+      pthread_mutex_unlock(&mfxt_lock);
+      for (unsigned i = 0; i < 6; i++)
+         [v[i] release];
+   }
+   return st;
+}
+
+void
+mtl_metalfx_temporal_destroy(uint64_t context)
+{
+   @autoreleasepool {
+      pthread_mutex_lock(&mfxt_lock);
+      for (unsigned i = 0; i < MFXT_ENTRIES; i++)
+         if (mfxt_entries[i].used && mfxt_entries[i].context == context)
+            mfxt_drop(&mfxt_entries[i]);
+      pthread_mutex_unlock(&mfxt_lock);
+   }
+}
+
+void
+mtl_metalfx_temporal_tail(mtl_device *device, mtl_command_buffer *cmd_buf)
+{
+   @autoreleasepool {
+      id<MTLDevice> dev = (id<MTLDevice>)device;
+      id<MTL4CommandBuffer> cb = (id<MTL4CommandBuffer>)cmd_buf;
+      /* A few bytes the encoder writes (a command, so that it waits and is
+       * waited for), in a residency set of their own; one per device. */
+      static struct {
+         id<MTLDevice> dev;
+         id<MTLBuffer> buf;
+         id<MTLResidencySet> set;
+      } tails[4];
+      id<MTLBuffer> buf = nil;
+      id<MTLResidencySet> set = nil;
+      pthread_mutex_lock(&mfxt_lock);
+      for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4 && !buf; i++) {
+         if (!tails[i].dev) {
+            MTLResidencySetDescriptor *rd = [MTLResidencySetDescriptor new];
+            NSError *err = nil;
+            id<MTLResidencySet> s =
+               [dev newResidencySetWithDescriptor:rd error:&err];
+            [rd release];
+            id<MTLBuffer> b =
+               [dev newBufferWithLength:16
+                                options:MTLResourceStorageModePrivate];
+            if (!s || !b) {
+               [s release];
+               [b release];
+               break;
+            }
+            [s addAllocation:b];
+            [s commit];
+            tails[i].dev = [dev retain];
+            tails[i].buf = b;
+            tails[i].set = s;
+         }
+         if (tails[i].dev == dev) {
+            buf = tails[i].buf;
+            set = tails[i].set;
+         }
+      }
+      pthread_mutex_unlock(&mfxt_lock);
+      if (!buf)
+         return;
+      [cb useResidencySet:set];
+      id<MTL4ComputeCommandEncoder> ce = [cb computeCommandEncoder];
+      [ce barrierAfterQueueStages:MTLStageAll
+                     beforeStages:MTLStageBlit
+                visibilityOptions:MTL4VisibilityOptionDevice];
+      [ce fillBuffer:buf range:NSMakeRange(0, 4) value:0];
+      [ce barrierAfterStages:MTLStageBlit
+           beforeQueueStages:MTLStageAll
+           visibilityOptions:MTL4VisibilityOptionDevice];
+      [ce endEncoding];
+   }
+}
